select public.prepify_load_bank('Computer Science', 7, $j$[["If a goal is \"precise and clear in setting up,\" it follows which part of the SMART framework?",["Measurable","Specific","Realistic","Achievable"],"B",3,1,"893603ed3451"],["A goal that is \"quantifiable and can be assessed\" is known as:",["Specific","Measurable","Time-Bound","Realistic"],"B",3,0,"0b40a65b7d66"],["\"Set attainable small goals which can be achieved\" is the definition of which SMART category?",["Specific","Achievable","Realistic","Time-Bound"],"B",3,0,"0d2c2272dc29"],["In a business plan, goals that are \"convincing in nature, not in the clouds\" are:",["Specific","Realistic","Time-Bound","Achievable"],"B",3,0,"ef362d484ddc"],["Why do SMART goals need to be \"Time-Bound\"?",["To ensure the founder works 24 hours a day.","Because strategies and goals need to be reviewed for improvement.","To close the business as soon as possible.","To make the goal sound more professional to banks."],"B",3,0,"d76911d4965a"],["If \"demand is great for the available supply,\" what is the logical action for profit?",["The price should be decreased immediately.","The price (and thus the profit) may be increased.","The business should stop selling the item.","The markup should be removed."],"B",3,0,"cd559e5e3647"],["Which of the following is a recognized \"Drawback\" of entrepreneurship?",["Having the power to gain control over one's own life.","Uncertainty of income and the risk of losing their investments.","The ability to make a difference in the world.","Becoming self-fulfilled through their professional work."],"B",3,0,"c1abf62d75f1"],["How is the \"Design Thinking\" process officially described?",["It is a simple, straight line where you never repeat a previous step.","It is an iterative and non-linear process that contains five phases.","It is a secret method that only professional artists are allowed to use.","It is a mathematical formula used only to find the cost of goods."],"B",3,0,"6f48b72d4630"],["During the \"Empathize\" phase, what is the main objective?",["Understand the user thoroughly within the context of your design challenge.","Pick the first idea you have and start selling it to the public immediately.","Calculate the total amount of money you need to borrow from a bank.","Design a very colorful logo using a digital tool like Canva."],"A",3,1,"751e9ed4f893"],["What is the goal of the \"Define\" phase in problem-solving?",["Brainstorm as many different ideas as you can in one hour.","Identify the right problem and create an actionable problem statement.","Build a very expensive and high-quality final version of your product.","Hire a team of experts to tell you what your users are thinking."],"B",3,0,"2792590fbee1"],["In the \"Ideate\" phase, entrepreneurs are encouraged to:",["Narrow down their options to only one single solution as fast as possible.","Come up with as many ideas as possible to solve the problem statement.","Stop thinking of new ideas once they find one that is very cheap.","Focus only on the ideas that their competitors are already using."],"B",3,0,"ec86214f213b"],["What is the strategic purpose of building a \"Prototype\"?",["To show the world that your business is already very successful and rich.","To build a sample model to learn fast, learn cheap and learn early.","To replace the need for ever talking to real customers in the future.","To create the final, permanent version of the product for the market."],"B",3,0,"26d75688a3bd"],["Why is the \"Test\" phase so important for the final solution?",["To collect feedback from users to refine the problem, solution and user needs.","To prove to the users that your first idea was already perfect.","To find out which of your employees is working the hardest.","To calculate the exact markup percentage for your new service."],"A",3,0,"1c03b44d5cb5"],["Which of the following shows the correct sequence of the five phases of Design Thinking?",["Define, Ideate, Empathize, Test, Prototype","Empathize, Define, Ideate, Prototype, Test","Ideate, Empathize, Prototype, Test, Define","Prototype, Test, Empathize, Define, Ideate"],"B",3,0,"4d91131d07f1"],["To find a realistic final Selling Price, what three things must an entrepreneur add together?",["Cost of Production + Overheads + Profit","Cost of Production + Competitor's Price + Profit","Overheads + Salary + Marketing Price","Only Cost of Production + Profit"],"A",3,0,"5f57b3d2dcff"],["A SWOT analysis is used to evaluate a product by examining which four core elements?",["Salary, Overheads, Production, and Profit","Advantages, Disadvantages, Possibilities, and Risks","Software, Templates, Workbooks, and Technology","Strategy, Supply, Sales, and Structure"],"B",3,0,"36da5ce83c20"],["Questions regarding the shape, size, and color of a product help a business understand why customers:",["Are willing to pay a commercial price","Need a specific hour of service","Like or dislike the product","Are classified by income status"],"C",3,0,"72328660abe2"],["If customers decide to stop buying a product completely, the market demand is considered:",["Sustainable","Unsustainable","Commercial","Regular"],"B",3,0,"16ce565a0a88"],["What is the main difference between \"Demand\" and \"Customers\"?",["Customers only need the product, but demand does not.","Customers are willing to pay for the product, while demand is just the need.","Demand represents the businesses, while customers represent the community.","There is no difference between them."],"B",3,0,"1d3c2dc9ac3e"],["If two different shopkeepers are selling similar items in the same market, they are called:",["Partners","Competitors","Customers","Surveyors"],"B",3,0,"5cee9a734caa"],["A business is considered \"Sustainable\" if the customers buy the product:",["Only one time.","Regularly or seasonally.","Never again.","Only when the price drops to zero."],"B",3,0,"d4178214a86f"],["Which of the following is defined as a free-to-use, online versatile app that lets users create stunning graphics, videos, and social media content?",["LivePlan","WordPress","Canva","Business PlanWriter"],"C",3,0,"de0874b92ac3"],["WordPress serves globally as an open-source tool specifically designed for:",["Operating System (OS)","Content Management System (CMS)","Database Management System (DBMS)","Graphic Design Suite"],"B",3,0,"99e25af8d7d2"],["Which entrepreneurial skill involves working with others and accepting individuals irrespective of their caste, gender, social status, or disability?",["Conducting myself","Interacting with people","Thinking","My safety and survival"],"B",3,0,"bf8940690266"],["Which comprehensive business planning software is purposefully designed to give you all the tools you need to create your business plan and present it?",["LivePlan","WordPress","Canva","Business PlanWriter"],"A",3,0,"e0be4af0e4da"],["Which specialized business planning application is a dedicated spreadsheet program that is a part of the SoftMaker Office suite?",["LivePlan","PlanWrite","PlanMaker","WordPress"],"C",3,0,"fad895572c9f"],["Which business planning software listed in the text is developed by Palo Alto Software?",["PlanMaker","Business Plan Pro","PlanWrite","WordPress"],"B",3,0,"d4a7671f1f48"],["Which of the following terms describes a person who starts, organizes, and manages a business while taking on financial risks for the sake of profit?",["Manager","Investor","Entrepreneur","Employee"],"C",3,0,"5c1001f13d3d"],["Which characteristic of an entrepreneur is the ability to keep going through failures and setbacks while staying focused on long-term goals?",["Desire for immediate feedback","Self-reliance","Determination (grit)","Future orientation"],"C",3,0,"3b30ae2ebab2"],["An entrepreneur shifts economic resources from an area of scarcity to one of higher productivity and greater yield. This mainly shows:",["Risk-taking ability","Innovative thinking","Resource allocation skills","Organizing capability"],"C",3,1,"ae18f18388d5"],["What distinguishes entrepreneurs from ordinary business owners in how they treat risk?",["They avoid all risk","They take moderate, calculated risks rather than wild gambles","They rely completely on others to decide","They focus only on short-term profit"],"B",3,0,"82b1a4cf236f"],["Many successful entrepreneurs failed several times before succeeding. Which trait explains why they kept trying?",["High level of energy","Confidence in their ability to succeed","Skill at organizing","Valuing achievement over money"],"B",3,1,"424327757224"],["In Design Thinking, the phase where entrepreneurs build a sample model to test their ideas is:",["Empathize","Define","Ideate","Prototype"],"D",1,0,"7e4e40f9a913"],["Design Thinking is \"iterative and non-linear\". This means:",["The steps must be followed strictly in order","Teams keep reviewing and improving their ideas based on results","Only one solution is developed at a time","The process ends after testing"],"B",3,0,"c227be51d43a"],["Which Design Thinking phase involves coming up with as many ideas as possible to solve the problem statement?",["Empathize","Define","Ideate","Test"],"C",1,0,"15cf1ad45498"],["A business plan acts as a \"game plan\" for running the business successfully during start-up. Which goal of a business plan is this?",["Attracting capital","Guiding the entrepreneur during launch","Comparing results against targets","Finding the main risks"],"B",3,0,"0ae1d80dca50"],["In the SMART framework, a \"time-bound\" goal means:",["The goal is about time management","A specific timeframe is set for achieving the result","The goal is measured in hours","Time is the only consideration"],"B",1,0,"7e4ef18c70d7"],["LivePlan, PlanMaker and Canva are examples of:",["Business financing options","Business planning software and tools","Government business licences","Marketing strategies"],"B",1,0,"4574b9943ee2"],["When demand for a product is high and supply is limited, an entrepreneur can:",["Decrease the price to attract customers","Increase the price and so the profit margin","Keep the same price regardless","Stop production to increase scarcity"],"B",3,1,"a2d25a2af9eb"],["Which is the formula for the selling price?",["Cost of production × overheads","Cost of production + overheads + profit","Cost of production − overheads + profit","Cost of production + overheads − profit"],"B",3,0,"8892dbc7607f"],["The people who need a product or service and are willing to pay for it are called:",["Competitors","Suppliers","Customers","Distributors"],"C",1,0,"8ec0683bf5f3"],["Businesses that provide similar products or services are called:",["Partners","Competitors","Customers","Investors"],"B",1,0,"815c960a2848"],["Which Sustainable Development Goal is about ensuring healthy lives and well-being for all at all ages?",["Goal 1: No Poverty","Goal 2: Zero Hunger","Goal 3: Good Health and Well-being","Goal 4: Quality Education"],"C",3,0,"64d3198fe214"],["\"Decent Work and Economic Growth\" is which Sustainable Development Goal?",["Goal 6","Goal 7","Goal 8","Goal 9"],"C",3,0,"345684c89a02"],["The skill group that includes creativity, problem-solving and decision-making is:",["Conducting oneself","Thinking skills","Interacting with people","Safety and survival skills"],"B",3,0,"5bbe74c41a45"],["An entrepreneur studies a community's needs and identifies products or services to solve its difficulties. This demonstrates:",["Self-reliance","Risk-taking","Opportunity recognition","Financial management"],"C",3,1,"7937b00f828f"],["Mr. Sharma runs a bakery with 10 employees. Mrs. Verma bakes cakes at home and sells them online by herself. Which statement is true?",["Only Mr. Sharma is an entrepreneur because he hires people","Only Mrs. Verma is an entrepreneur because she works alone","Both are entrepreneurs because they organize resources and bear risk to make a profit","Neither is, because baking is a traditional job"],"C",5,1,"df7f32b07aa7"],["\"Innovation\" in entrepreneurship means:",["Copying a foreign product exactly","Doing what everyone else does, but cheaper","Introducing a new method, product or idea that creates value","Focusing only on money"],"C",3,0,"119bd46dd796"],["Which scenario carries the HIGHEST level of risk?",["Working as a cashier in a grocery store","Investing one's life savings in a new restaurant in an untested location","Buying government bonds","Freelancing for established clients"],"B",3,1,"191cb5594f6a"],["An entrepreneur who lacks financial literacy is most likely to fail because of:",["Poor product design","Mismanaging cash flow and being unable to budget costs","Excellent customer service","Too many employees"],"B",3,1,"ae51c59a419d"],["Ahmed, 22, has designed logos for friends for three years, notices that local small businesses use outdated logos, and starts his own design business with savings of PKR 50,000. Which trait is he mainly showing by starting his own business?",["Preference for moderate risk","Desire for responsibility","Skill at organizing","High level of energy"],"B",5,1,"bcd5551fbb80"],["Ahmed starts a graphic design business because he noticed that small businesses in his community lack professional logos. Which step in developing a business idea does this relate to?",["Identifying a need in the community","Calculating production costs","Analyzing competitors","Setting profit margins"],"A",3,1,"74c7e6b6b77c"],["Ahmed wants to use Design Thinking to develop his new graphic design service. Which phase should he begin with?",["Prototype","Test","Empathize","Ideate"],"C",3,1,"28cf716861c5"],["Improving entrepreneurial skills and knowledge through training and structured programmes is called:",["Human resource management","Entrepreneurship development","Financial auditing","Market saturation"],"B",3,0,"539cbd710f56"],["A business that sells tangible goods such as paints or cars is mainly a:",["Service business","Product business (manufacturing or trading)","Hybrid business","Non-governmental organization"],"B",3,0,"683581725f40"],["Four friends start a food delivery service: one cooks, one markets, one handles logistics and one manages money. Dividing the work by each person's skill shows which characteristic?",["Desire for immediate feedback","Self-reliance","Skill at organizing","Future orientation"],"C",5,1,"05251cf93670"],["Four friends starting a food delivery service use Canva for their menu, WordPress for their website and LivePlan for their business proposal. They are using:",["Government support programmes","Business planning software and tools","Financial institutions","Marketing agencies"],"B",3,1,"ccd7bca4d0b5"],["Friends planning a food delivery service survey how many people in their city would use it. They are trying to estimate their:",["Profit margin","Market size","Production costs","Competitors' prices"],"B",3,1,"92a88b1816fa"],["When a product is popular but only a few are available, an entrepreneur can usually:",["lower the price","raise the price and increase the profit margin","stop selling it","give it away free"],"B",3,1,"a2d25a2af9eb"],["The first phase of Design Thinking is:",["Prototype","Test","Empathize","Ideate"],"C",1,0,"28cf716861c5"],["In the SMART goal framework, the \"M\" stands for:",["Measurable","Modern","Monthly","Manual"],"A",3,0,"7e4ef18c70d7"],["Which option carries the LOWEST level of financial risk?",["Buying government savings bonds","Investing all savings in a new, untested business","Opening a shop in an area with no customers","Borrowing heavily to start a factory"],"A",3,1,"191cb5594f6a"],["WordPress is widely used to build and manage websites. It is a:",["Content Management System","Database Management System","operating system","spreadsheet"],"A",3,0,"99e25af8d7d2"],["Before opening a juice stall, Sana counts how many people pass her street every day who might buy juice. She is estimating her:",["profit margin","market size","production cost","tax"],"B",3,1,"92a88b1816fa"],["The cost of making a bag is Rs 400, overheads are Rs 100 and the desired profit is Rs 150. Using selling price = cost + overheads + profit, the selling price is:",["Rs 450","Rs 500","Rs 650","Rs 550"],"C",5,1,"8892dbc7607f"],["In Design Thinking, the phase where you build a simple model of your idea to try out is:",["Empathize","Define","Prototype","Ideate"],"C",3,0,"4d91131d07f1"],["Introducing a new product or method that creates value for customers is called:",["imitation","innovation","inflation","investment"],"B",1,0,"119bd46dd796"]]$j$::jsonb, true);
select public.prepify_load_bank('English', 1, $j$[["The title \"Rahmatul-lil-Alameen\" means:",["Mercy for all the worlds","Leader of the Arabs","The last messenger","The truthful one"],"A",1,0,"8b45f643982b"],["Before prophethood, the people of Makkah called the Holy Prophet ﷺ \"Al-Amin\", which means:",["The trustworthy","The brave","The wise","The generous"],"A",1,0,"4da94b15960f"],["Choose the synonym of \"compassion\":",["Cruelty","Sympathy","Anger","Pride"],"B",1,0,"b3a76e444825"],["Choose the antonym of \"mercy\":",["Kindness","Pity","Cruelty","Grace"],"C",1,0,"13abbc9478cc"],["Choose the correct spelling:",["Forgivness","Forgiveness","Forgiviness","Forgeveness"],"B",1,0,"9d17c5e6e690"],["In \"The Holy Prophet ﷺ forgave the people of Taif\", the verb is:",["Holy","forgave","people","Taif"],"B",1,0,"b33158e0b3a4"],["Choose the passive voice of \"He forgave his enemies.\":",["His enemies are forgiven by him.","His enemies were forgiven by him.","His enemies had forgiven him.","His enemies were forgiving by him."],"B",3,0,"603dff3cffb5"],["Which of these words is a noun?",["Merciful","Mercifully","Mercy","Merciless"],"C",1,0,"929483b14eee"],["The adjective form of \"humility\" is:",["Humble","Humbly","Humbleness","Humiliate"],"A",3,0,"7f26a53851fe"],["Sara wants one word for a person who always keeps promises and can be depended on. Which word should she use?",["Reliable","Careless","Arrogant","Stubborn"],"A",3,1,"50c0627f9a45"],["Fill in the blank: The Holy Prophet ﷺ was kind ___ everyone.",["at","to","on","over"],"B",3,0,"79643fcc6327"],["In the Last Sermon, the Holy Prophet ﷺ declared that an Arab has no superiority over a non-Arab except by:",["wealth","piety and good action","family name","language"],"B",3,0,"3af31ba5a155"],["In \"He treated orphans kindly\", the word \"kindly\" is:",["a noun","an adjective","an adverb","a verb"],"C",3,0,"c67d43dcda89"],["Choose the correctly punctuated sentence:",["The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Be kind to others.\"","The Prophet ﷺ said \"be kind to others\".","The Prophet ﷺ said, be kind to others.","the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Be kind to others.\""],"A",3,0,"792680074042"],["The plural of \"orphan\" is:",["orphanes","orphans","orphen","orphanage"],"B",1,0,"aeda6f07611f"],["Choose the correct verb: Neither the students nor the teacher ___ absent.",["were","are","was","have"],"C",5,0,"6a174321c57c"],["\"Tolerance\" means:",["accepting views different from one's own","the habit of complaining","the desire for revenge","the fear of strangers"],"A",3,0,"4d75b34337f8"],["After the Conquest of Makkah, the Holy Prophet ﷺ pardoned his former enemies. This action best shows his:",["forgiveness","strictness","wealth","silence"],"A",3,1,"309a65ea0025"],["Choose the correct sentence:",["He don't tell lies.","He doesn't tells lies.","He doesn't tell lies.","He not tell lies."],"C",3,0,"2467a7b71b0e"],["Which sentence is in the past perfect tense?",["He helps the poor.","He had helped the poor.","He was helping the poor.","He will help the poor."],"B",3,0,"2afad6958a72"],["Choose the synonym of \"benevolent\":",["Kind-hearted","Selfish","Lazy","Rude"],"A",3,0,"9543a3af63ca"],["Choose the antonym of \"honest\":",["Truthful","Sincere","Dishonest","Upright"],"C",1,0,"27d96e58020a"],["The word \"unjust\" is formed by adding the prefix:",["in-","un-","dis-","mis-"],"B",1,0,"a3f70f20d73e"],["Fill in the blank with the correct article: He was ___ honest man.",["a","an","the","no article"],"B",3,0,"574f6cdf51cd"],["Choose the indirect speech of: He said, \"I respect my elders.\"",["He said that he respected his elders.","He said that I respect my elders.","He says that he respected his elders.","He said that he respects my elders."],"A",5,0,"7831c62d2ca9"],["Ahmed sees a classmate being teased unfairly and stands up for him. Which quality from the lesson is Ahmed showing?",["Justice and kindness","Greed","Laziness","Pride"],"A",3,1,"ecd45e92cef1"],["\"Humble\" is the opposite of:",["modest","proud","gentle","simple"],"B",3,0,"20b44162a14a"],["Which of these is a compound word?",["Kindness","Mankind","Kindly","Unkind"],"B",5,0,"c3b6464321ee"],["Choose the correct preposition: Muslims believe in the Holy Prophet ﷺ ___ the last messenger of Allah.",["like","as","for","by"],"B",5,0,"2058880e6424"],["The word \"sermon\" means:",["a religious speech","a poem","a letter","a story"],"A",1,0,"1d55cf2b907e"],["A shopkeeper always returns extra money that customers pay him by mistake. Which word best describes him?",["Trustworthy","Wasteful","Jealous","Timid"],"A",3,1,"03db0f93e358"],["Choose the correctly spelled word:",["Tolerence","Tolerance","Tollerance","Tolarance"],"B",3,0,"220821433d08"],["\"The Holy Prophet ﷺ was sent as a mercy for all creation.\" This sentence is in the:",["active voice","passive voice","imperative mood","interrogative form"],"B",5,0,"4146a4855eb8"],["Fill in the blank: Honesty is the ___ policy.",["good","better","best","most good"],"C",1,0,"f30d3a9b873a"],["Which sentence is a command?",["He is kind.","Be kind to animals.","Is he kind?","How kind he is!"],"B",1,0,"ead5aded9e6e"],["Choose the word closest in meaning to \"justice\":",["Fairness","Weakness","Loudness","Laziness"],"A",3,0,"6f0bdba4b886"],["Choose the correct sentence:",["Everyone love the Prophet ﷺ.","Everyone loves the Prophet ﷺ.","Everyone are loving the Prophet ﷺ.","Everyone have loved the Prophet ﷺ."],"B",5,0,"135baf67e7cf"],["A student writes: \"The Prophet ﷺ taught us to treat our neighbours well.\" What is the tense of \"taught\"?",["Simple present","Simple past","Past continuous","Present perfect"],"B",3,0,"8114a3a6da73"],["Choose the indirect speech of: She said, \"I help my neighbours.\"",["She said that she helped her neighbours.","She said that I help my neighbours.","She says that she helped her neighbours.","She said that she helps my neighbours."],"A",5,0,"7831c62d2ca9"],["A student returns a lost wallet to its owner without taking anything. Which word best describes the student?",["Honest","Greedy","Lazy","Rude"],"A",1,1,"03db0f93e358"],["Fill in the blank with the correct article: She is ___ obedient daughter.",["a","an","the","no article"],"B",3,0,"574f6cdf51cd"],["Choose the correctly spelled word:",["Forgivness","Forgiveness","Forgiviness","Forgivenes"],"B",3,0,"220821433d08"],["Choose the passive voice of \"He helped the poor.\":",["The poor are helped by him.","The poor were helped by him.","The poor had helped him.","The poor was helped by him."],"B",3,0,"603dff3cffb5"],["Choose the correct sentence:",["She don't waste food.","She doesn't wastes food.","She doesn't waste food.","She not waste food."],"C",3,0,"2467a7b71b0e"],["Choose the antonym of \"kindness\":",["Gentleness","Care","Cruelty","Mercy"],"C",1,0,"13abbc9478cc"],["In \"The Prophet ﷺ forgave the people of Makkah\", the tense of \"forgave\" is:",["simple present","simple past","past continuous","present perfect"],"B",3,0,"8114a3a6da73"],["The adjective form of \"mercy\" is:",["Merciful","Mercifully","Mercies","Mercy"],"A",3,0,"7f26a53851fe"],["A person who stays calm and does not complain while waiting is:",["patient","proud","jealous","careless"],"A",1,1,"50c0627f9a45"]]$j$::jsonb, true);
select public.prepify_load_bank('English', 2, $j$[["An \"entrepreneur\" is a person who:",["starts and runs a business, taking on its risks","works only for the government","avoids all kinds of risk","buys goods only for personal use"],"A",1,0,"d3301e46d5bc"],["Hazrat Khadija (RA) is remembered as a successful:",["poet","merchant","soldier","teacher"],"B",1,0,"fb501d81ea85"],["Hazrat Khadija (RA) hired the Holy Prophet ﷺ to lead her trade caravan to:",["Egypt","Syria","Yemen","Persia"],"B",3,0,"e44616f57267"],["Choose the synonym of \"venture\":",["Enterprise","Holiday","Failure","Rest"],"A",3,0,"d6f67163246a"],["Choose the antonym of \"profit\":",["Gain","Income","Loss","Benefit"],"C",1,0,"74a139f29315"],["Choose the correct spelling:",["Entrepreneur","Entreprenuer","Enterpreneur","Entrepeneur"],"A",3,0,"22d47f109f9c"],["The noun form of \"independent\" is:",["Independently","Independence","Depend","Dependable"],"B",3,0,"1ee45a4d8490"],["\"Empowerment\" means:",["giving someone the confidence and means to control their own life","taking away someone's rights","making someone lazy","forcing someone to stop working"],"A",3,0,"67df3245e7ff"],["Ayesha sells handmade jewellery online from home and manages her own orders and profits. She is best described as:",["an employee","a home-based entrepreneur","a customer","a supplier's agent"],"B",3,1,"2380e6bf99ca"],["Fill in the blank: She invested her savings ___ a small bakery.",["at","in","on","by"],"B",3,0,"71108b6f76c6"],["In \"She manages her business wisely\", the word \"wisely\" is:",["a noun","a verb","an adverb","an adjective"],"C",1,0,"52183314a415"],["Choose the passive voice of \"She started a new business.\":",["A new business is started by her.","A new business was started by her.","A new business has been started by her.","A new business was starting by her."],"B",3,0,"fd2ecfd51cda"],["Choose the correct sentence:",["She have started a shop.","She has started a shop.","She has start a shop.","She having started a shop."],"B",1,0,"47368e84686d"],["Which sentence is in the present perfect tense?",["She sells clothes.","She sold clothes.","She has sold many clothes.","She will sell clothes."],"C",3,0,"71e7d2f30270"],["The word \"capital\" in business means:",["the money used to start or run a business","a big letter","the main city of a country","a type of building"],"A",3,0,"0d5136c4d3ab"],["Choose the synonym of \"initiative\":",["Enterprise and self-motivation","Laziness","Delay","Fear"],"A",3,0,"a16631efd4ff"],["A woman borrows a small loan, buys a sewing machine and starts stitching clothes for her neighbours. Which quality does she mainly show?",["Self-reliance","Dependence","Carelessness","Idleness"],"A",3,1,"7d53fdf9903e"],["Choose the correct article: She opened ___ online store last year.",["a","an","the","no article"],"B",3,0,"917e118d49bf"],["Choose the correct form: If she works hard, she ___ succeed.",["will","would","had","was"],"A",5,0,"a4acd6ee43f5"],["Which word is an adjective?",["Success","Succeed","Successful","Successfully"],"C",1,0,"cd87e609330f"],["Choose the antonym of \"confident\":",["Bold","Sure","Nervous","Brave"],"C",3,0,"9915270eaf64"],["Choose the indirect speech of: She said, \"I will open a boutique.\"",["She said that she would open a boutique.","She said that I will open a boutique.","She says that she would open a boutique.","She said that she will opened a boutique."],"A",5,0,"e10d151145b4"],["Choose the correctly punctuated sentence:",["Her shop sells clothes, shoes and bags.","Her shop sells, clothes shoes and bags.","Her shop sells clothes shoes, and bags","her shop sells clothes, shoes and bags."],"A",3,0,"ce24877b21f9"],["The prefix in \"unemployed\" means:",["again","not","before","after"],"B",1,0,"effac9fd4964"],["Sana's online business grows because customers trust the quality of her products. Which quality is most important here?",["Honesty and quality","Rudeness","Delay","High prices"],"A",3,1,"8be6f25f5f4f"],["Choose the correct preposition: Muslim women have contributed ___ trade since early Islamic times.",["to","at","from","over"],"A",5,0,"1a0e0dd94c9e"],["\"Economic independence\" means:",["being able to support oneself financially","having no money at all","depending on others for money","spending carelessly"],"A",3,0,"691376bd5f1e"],["Choose the plural of \"business\":",["businesss","businesses","business's","busineses"],"B",1,0,"fe84bc9e1109"],["Choose the word that best completes the sentence: Starting a business requires hard work and ___.",["determination","determined","determine","determinedly"],"A",5,0,"fa3ac9caa564"],["Which sentence is a question?",["She runs a café.","Does she run a café?","Run the café well.","What a lovely café!"],"B",1,0,"0211134011fb"],["Maria makes a plan listing her costs, prices and expected customers before opening her shop. What is she preparing?",["A business plan","A recipe","A holiday plan","A complaint"],"A",3,1,"971ff47c97a3"],["Choose the synonym of \"flourish\":",["Fail","Prosper","Shrink","Collapse"],"B",3,0,"6fc35586982b"],["Hina's bakery gains loyal customers because she never sells stale bread. Which quality helps her business most?",["Honesty and quality","Rudeness","Delay","High prices"],"A",1,1,"8be6f25f5f4f"],["The prefix in \"unhappy\" means:",["again","not","before","after"],"B",1,0,"effac9fd4964"],["Choose the synonym of \"prosper\":",["Fail","Flourish","Shrink","Collapse"],"B",3,0,"6fc35586982b"],["Fill in the blank: He invested his money ___ a clothing shop.",["at","in","on","by"],"B",3,0,"71108b6f76c6"],["Choose the antonym of \"nervous\":",["Anxious","Worried","Confident","Afraid"],"C",3,0,"9915270eaf64"],["The noun form of \"succeed\" is:",["Successful","Success","Successfully","Succeeding"],"B",3,0,"1ee45a4d8490"],["Choose the correct form: If he saves money, he ___ buy a sewing machine.",["will","would","had","was"],"A",5,0,"a4acd6ee43f5"],["Choose the passive voice of \"She opened a new shop.\":",["A new shop is opened by her.","A new shop was opened by her.","A new shop has been opened by her.","A new shop was open by her."],"B",3,0,"fd2ecfd51cda"],["Zara bakes cakes at home and sells them to neighbours, keeping her own accounts. She is best described as:",["an employee","a home-based entrepreneur","a customer","a supplier"],"B",3,1,"2380e6bf99ca"],["Before starting a tailoring shop, Rabia writes down her costs, prices and target customers. She is preparing:",["a business plan","a recipe","a travel plan","a complaint"],"A",1,1,"971ff47c97a3"]]$j$::jsonb, true);
select public.prepify_load_bank('English', 3, $j$[["\"Globalization\" means:",["the growing connection of countries through trade, technology and culture","the separation of countries from each other","the study of maps","building walls between nations"],"A",1,0,"59ab844af148"],["The expression \"global village\" suggests that:",["the world has become closely connected through communication","everyone lives in villages","villages are growing larger","cities are disappearing"],"A",3,0,"6ecb95f3b9e8"],["Choose the synonym of \"connect\":",["Link","Break","Divide","Separate"],"A",1,0,"a574f22e8fbc"],["Choose the antonym of \"modern\":",["New","Recent","Ancient","Current"],"C",1,0,"79a22c5b4017"],["Choose the correct spelling:",["Technology","Tecnology","Technolegy","Tecknology"],"A",1,0,"d375851dce8c"],["Buying and selling goods over the internet is called:",["e-commerce","e-mail","e-book","e-learning"],"A",1,0,"153b0c420ddc"],["In \"The internet has changed our lives\", the tense is:",["simple past","present perfect","past perfect","simple present"],"B",3,0,"8edb9ec3cbbd"],["Choose the passive voice of \"People use smartphones everywhere.\":",["Smartphones are used everywhere by people.","Smartphones were used everywhere by people.","Smartphones used everywhere by people.","Smartphones are using everywhere by people."],"A",3,0,"b598451c545c"],["Hamza orders a book from another country and receives it at home in a week. Which feature of the modern world makes this possible?",["Global trade and online shopping","Letter writing","Barter system","Local markets only"],"A",3,1,"26777c68741a"],["Fill in the blank: We are connected ___ the whole world through the internet.",["at","with","on","by"],"B",3,0,"bf96e0ad229a"],["The gap between people who have access to modern technology and those who do not is called the:",["digital divide","digital age","global village","information highway"],"A",3,0,"e12bd9ea42fb"],["Choose the word that is an adverb:",["Rapid","Rapidly","Rapidity","Rapidness"],"B",1,0,"aba908588eef"],["Choose the correct sentence:",["Technology make life easier.","Technology makes life easier.","Technology making life easier.","Technology have made life easier."],"B",1,0,"7dcd1de071fd"],["Choose the synonym of \"rapid\":",["Slow","Quick","Weak","Late"],"B",1,0,"eff5f7aa12b9"],["Which word is a noun?",["Communicate","Communication","Communicative","Communicatively"],"B",1,0,"9334877cc276"],["Choose the indirect speech of: He said, \"The world is changing fast.\"",["He said that the world was changing fast.","He said that the world is changed fast.","He says that the world was changing fast.","He said the world changing fast."],"A",5,0,"d0068f394a15"],["A student in Karachi attends a live online class taught by a teacher in London. This is an example of:",["distance learning made possible by technology","a traditional classroom","a postal service","a printed newspaper"],"A",3,1,"197950b23677"],["Choose the correctly punctuated sentence:",["Did you check your email today?","did you check your email today?","Did you check your email today.","Did you check, your email today?"],"A",3,0,"b2b6027a4876"],["Choose the correct article: The internet is ___ useful invention.",["a","an","the","no article"],"A",5,0,"7cbd6b04f065"],["Choose the antonym of \"advantage\":",["Benefit","Profit","Disadvantage","Gain"],"C",1,0,"c33a9f37244a"],["Fill in the blank: Social media has both benefits ___ drawbacks.",["or","and","but","nor"],"B",1,0,"e52c85b159b8"],["Choose the correct form: By next year, more people ___ online shopping.",["will have used","have used","had used","using"],"A",5,0,"1fe04934e823"],["The prefix \"inter-\" in \"international\" means:",["between","under","against","without"],"A",3,0,"28725de1eb71"],["Nida spends so many hours on social media that she neglects her studies. This shows a:",["negative effect of technology misuse","benefit of technology","healthy habit","study technique"],"A",3,1,"deb42b328803"],["Choose the plural of \"medium\" as used in \"mass media\":",["mediums only","media","medias","mediumes"],"B",5,0,"981d11b39e34"],["Choose the synonym of \"information\":",["Knowledge","Ignorance","Silence","Confusion"],"A",1,0,"9a80d476764f"],["Which sentence is in the future continuous tense?",["We will use robots.","We will be using robots.","We will have used robots.","We are using robots."],"B",3,0,"ce162a7fa2e4"],["Choose the word that best completes the sentence: Online banking is fast and ___.",["convenient","convenience","conveniently","convene"],"A",3,0,"71b3f4223c5b"],["An online shop in Lahore sells its products to customers in Dubai and Toronto. This shows that modern businesses can reach:",["a global market","only local customers","only relatives","no customers"],"A",3,1,"8d134d54a135"],["Choose the adjective in: \"Smart devices are changing the world.\"",["Smart","devices","changing","world"],"A",1,0,"5cbb2ecfb0fb"],["Choose the indirect speech of: She said, \"Technology is useful.\"",["She said that technology was useful.","She said that technology is used.","She says that technology was useful.","She said that technology will be useful."],"A",5,0,"d0068f394a15"],["In \"Mobile phones have made life easier\", the tense is:",["simple past","present perfect","past perfect","simple present"],"B",3,0,"8edb9ec3cbbd"],["Choose the antonym of \"ancient\":",["Old","Historic","Modern","Aged"],"C",1,0,"79a22c5b4017"],["Choose the correct article: A computer is ___ amazing machine.",["a","an","the","no article"],"B",5,0,"7cbd6b04f065"],["Fill in the blank: The internet has advantages ___ disadvantages.",["or","and","but","nor"],"B",1,0,"e52c85b159b8"],["Choose the word that is an adverb:",["Quick","Quickly","Quickness","Quicken"],"B",1,0,"aba908588eef"],["A student spends all night playing online games and falls asleep in class. This shows a:",["negative effect of technology misuse","benefit of technology","healthy habit","study technique"],"A",3,1,"deb42b328803"],["A small Sialkot company sells footballs to buyers in Europe through its website. This shows businesses can reach:",["a global market","only local customers","only relatives","nobody"],"A",3,1,"8d134d54a135"],["Choose the plural of \"phenomenon\":",["phenomenons","phenomena","phenomenas","phenomenon"],"B",5,0,"981d11b39e34"]]$j$::jsonb, true);
